The numbers is a list of 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, and 3.
The wanted is 2.
The counts is an empty map.
For each value in numbers.
Add 1 to entry value of counts.

The distinct is an empty list of whole numbers.
For each value in numbers.
If distinct contains value, skip to the next one.
Place value into distinct.

The last is the last position of distinct.
For every left from 0 to last.
For every right from left to last.
The leftvalue is item left of distinct.
The rightvalue is item right of distinct.
The leftcount is entry leftvalue of counts.
The rightcount is entry rightvalue of counts.
If rightcount is more than leftcount, swap item left of distinct and item right of distinct.

For every spot from 0 to wanted minus 1.
Show item spot of distinct.
